# qint: finite unions of half-open rational intervals.
#
# See demos/README.md for how to run this script.

# A qint constant is a union of half-open intervals, so joins and meets stay
# inside the algebra:

{[0, 1) | [2, 3)}:qint
n {[0, 1)}:qint | {[1, 2)}:qint
n {[0, 1)}:qint & {[1/2, 2)}:qint

# Complement reaches the infinite ends of the line:

n {[0, 1)}:qint'

# solve answers with a constant, and sat decides a system over the type:

solve x:qint != 0
sat x:qint != 0 && x:qint != 1

# The algebra is atomless: every nonzero constant splits into two smaller
# nonzero ones. A stream carries the same constants:

run 3 steps G (o1[t]:qint = {[0, 1)}:qint)
stop

quit
